prompt-patch.diff: the proposed teacher-line writer and TTS-compiler change (TALKING-RULES.md section 1.3 and section 2), 2026-10-04
====================================================================================================================

For the main loop to apply: `git apply docs/research/voice/v4/prompt-patch.diff`. `git apply --check` was clean against
the live tree at 19:40 UTC on 2026-10-04. Nothing under server/ or src/ was edited by this workstream.
This patch is a SUPERSET of talking-rules.patch, so apply one or the other, not both.

STATUS: nobody has heard speech produced by this code path. The round-3 renders (renders/manifest.json) are the
evidence for the direction. Arms B, C and D used hand-written lines and plans (lines.mjs), not this code.
The decision belongs to the round-3 ear test (TALKING-RULES section 6).

WRITER (the words she says)
- shapes.js: SPOKEN_SHAPE (one telegraphic shape per situation: think, correct, success, wonder, explain, greet,
  effort, ask, and joke), plus situationOf(move) and spokenNote(). These are shapes, never lines: no Hindi word, marker,
  praise phrase or quote. A test enforces this, under repo law `recited-prompt`.
- compile.js: a heard turn gets a "- said aloud (a note, not words to say): ..." line in the MOVE section.
  - Droppable at SPOKEN_DROP 4.5: it sheds after brief callbacks, wins, interests and vibe, and before relationship,
    misconceptions and content. It sheds instead of ever making a section throw.
  - The voice lane's reply answers a branch, so its note covers both outcomes: right → success, otherwise → correct.
  - The joke shape rides on every heard turn, because a child may joke on any turn.
- FIX vs talking-rules.patch: the cascade lane is the one DragonHD Diya actually speaks, and it compiles as lane "text"
  (instructions.js: state.mode "cascade" → "text"). talking-rules.patch gated SPOKEN_NOTE on lane === "voice", so the
  Diya lane never got it. Here, instructions.js passes spoken: true for voice and cascade. The screen-read text lane
  gets neither note.
- Budget, measured over every kit file with the first 4 items of every topic: 3 languages × 2 age bands × 4 variants
  (cascade rung 0/3, voice rung 0/3), with a full-size brief. That is 79,680 compiles.
  - The note was shed 0 times. No other part was newly shed. No BudgetError.
  - It adds 105 estimated tokens (156 on a voiced voice turn, which carries both branch shapes).
  - Script: probe/measure-spoken-note.mjs.
- NOT measured: whether the model follows a mid-prompt note. The last section has no room, and position is mechanism:
  a rule buried mid-brief fired 0 times in 8 in html-portfolio. The next step is a fire-rate eval of the said-aloud
  line on the cascade lane: generate replies per situation and score the echo, the key word last and the feeling held.
- NOT in this patch: the Roman → Devanagari step for the Hindi words before DragonHD (TALKING-RULES section 5.3). Diya
  read पैंतीस as "पेंटीज" 4 of 4 times from Roman input. Every v3 and v4 render was made from Devanagari the Director
  never writes. This step blocks any live gain on numbers.

TTS COMPILER (delivery plan to DragonHD SSML)
- From talking-rules.patch:
  - PACE_DELTA.brisk 0;
  - CALM_PITCH -8;
  - breakFor(): a planned pause P is written as a break of P-200 ms, and nothing is written under 250 ms;
  - think-aloud commaPause off;
  - Hindi think fillers हम्म and उम्म → अच्छा and चलो.
- moment.js rows follow the section 1.3 delivery rules:
  - every sentence pause inside a part is at least 300 ms (a sentence end with no break gets ~70 ms, the "reading"
    pause);
  - think-aloud ends at the base rate;
  - correction lowers pitch on its opening sentence only (pitchScope "first");
  - a wonder hook starts slow at -8 % pitch;
  - success (insight) is slower on the method;
  - joke (laughter) gets pivotPause 550-650 ms before the clause that turns back to the fact.
- align.js:
  - echoIndex() gives a 300-550 ms beat after a short turn-initial echo question of the child's words. It mirrors
    say.js isUptakeQuestion.
  - PIVOT is a closed per-language list of pivot words.
  - Per-clause pitch is 0 or -8, scoped by the row. Safety is always 0.
- dhd.js:
  - compileDhd follows clause.pitch, not the emotion. A "reassuring" middle clause no longer drops pitch.
  - clausesValid() is a fail-closed validator: a known pace, pitch 0 or -8..-20, a pause of 0..3000 ms, no markup.
    render.js speaks an invalid part plain and counts voice.expr.plan_invalid.
- render.js FIX vs talking-rules.patch: preludeRender stripped / pitch="-6%"/ as a string. With CALM_PITCH at -8, the
  uptake prelude would silently have gone out at -8 %. It now passes pitch 0 explicitly.
- governor.js: a per-row silence budget, plan.silenceCap:
  - think-aloud 3.0 s;
  - correction and wonder 2.5 s;
  - joke and success 1.8 s;
  - every other row keeps 1.5 s;
  - hard ceiling SILENCE_CAP_MAX_MS 3.0 s.
  These are proposals, to be settled by ear. The arm C renders carried 1.3-2.7 s of pause per line (screen
  pause_total_s).
- shared/contracts.ts: DeliveryClause.pitch?.
- KNOWN GAP, rate: production baseRate is -35 % (w2g-base-rate-minus-35), measured on ROMAN-script input. The v4 renders
  used Devanagari at -10 / -20 % absolute. -35 plus slow -10 = -45 %, and the v4 caps probe saw a clause pushed past
  about -30 % gain extra 100-290 ms gaps. When the Devanagari step lands, that decision's own reversal condition fires:
  re-run evals/tts-pace.mjs on Devanagari before trusting any pace in this patch.

TESTS
- New: tests/voice-talking-rules.test.mjs (8 tests). It covers the dhd.js and moment.js edits that talking-rules.patch
  shipped with no test.
- Updated: compiler, director-truth, voice-cascade-lane and voice-expressive-governor tests.
- On a scratch copy: 22 relevant test files, 202 tests, 199 pass, 0 fail, 3 browser-only not run.
  - The unpatched baseline was 192 tests, 188 pass, and the same browser files.
  - The full `node --test tests/` in the scratch copy has the same failure set patched and unpatched, apart from the
    new tests: 988 env failures (a missing evals/live-studio goldens file aborts the shared process), and every
    compiler test is in that set both ways.
  - Run the real gates on the live tree before committing: `npx tsc -b && npx vite build && npm test`.

